<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Manolada</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1316</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Manolada was fought on 5 July 1316 in Elis, in the north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a>, between rival claimants to the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-of-burgundy">Louis of Burgundy</a> defeated and killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-of-majorca">Ferdinand of Majorca</a>, who had invaded the principality on behalf of his infant son.</p></div>
